    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506-a1-a4">

                <pb facs="0564" n="1242" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1242"/>

                <head>A 4, No. 39.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 21, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Colleague:</hi> On the day of the departure
                    of the Prussian minister, but after he had left the city, I received from him a
                    note, a copy of which I enclose herewith.</p>
                <p>In compliance with the request contained in the note of the Prussian minister, I
                    have to ask that you will meet the members of the diplomatic corps, now in this
                    city, at my rooms, (Calle Donceles, No. 23,) on Monday, the 23d instant, at 12
                    o’clock m., there and then to take into consideration the request contained in
                    Mr. Wagner’s note.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your friend and colleague,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS CORWIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
